[00:03.60] House for Everyone (Mason)
[00:17.12] My bed is made of candy floss, the house is made of cheese
[00:24.39] It's lit by lots of glow-worms; if I'm wrong correct me please.
[00:28.06] The village is a pop-up book, the people wooden dolls.
[00:40.62] The roads are made of treacle things, it's time that I moved on.
[00:44.23] Chorus:
[00:52.45] My home is half a walnut shell, the journey will be long
[00:56.00] So I filled the whole with peppermints and creamy pink blanc-mange.
[01:00.51] I sailed away for fifteen days, it never once got dark
[01:04.14] And came upon two large houses set out in a park.
[01:07.70] Verse:
[01:08.64] On the door of one was truth, on the other door was lies.
[01:11.32] Which one should I enter thru? I really must decide
[01:15.97] The door of lies had lots of flowers growing round outside
[01:19.51] But looking close I noticed it was crumbling inside
[01:23.13] Verse:
[01:24.02] The door of truth was very plain, but stood up very strong,
[01:26.73] And when I entered thru its door I knew I wasn't wrong.
[01:35.71] 